  For each invented word, take its last subword's layer-0 embedding
  and compute cosine similarity to each canonical's embedding.
  If a Condition-2 layer's invented-word landings track last-subword
  embedding similarity (i.e., the closest canonical at layer 0 ==
  the predicted canonical at that layer), the layer's result is a
  propagated-token-identity artifact rather than a structural finding.

